6:["$","div",null,{"className":"prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-6","children":"Niskama Karma is one of the most practical and transformative teachings of the Bhagavad Gita. It does not mean passive action or lack of care. Rather, it means giving oneself completely to right action while relinquishing egoic insistence on reward, control, and outcome. This transforms work from a source of bondage into a path of purification."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"italic border-l-2 border-primary/20 pl-6 py-2","children":"Niskama Karma is the operational heart of Karma Yoga. It bridges ethics, action, and liberation by showing how worldly responsibility can become a vehicle for inner freedom."}]]}]
